            "review_text": "blueoceanvn\n60 contributions\n0\nCould do better\nMar 2015 • Couples\nNice interior design, staff service was nice and friendly. The main selections are steaks, not much else. Can't complain about that since it's branded as a steak house :)\n\nMy wife and I ordered rib-eye and strip loin, medium rare for both. One served with fries, the other with mashed potatoes and some veggie on the side. The fries were rather dried and over-cooked. Smashed potatoes tasted ok. The steak were cooked as ordered and tasted good. \n\nMaybe our visit was during a promo month, after the meal we were offered deserts which was Panna cota in a small jar. To be honest, it tasted like flan. Other than Panna Cota, only seasonal fruits were offered as desert on the menu which is disappointing for those who're used to having some ice-cream or pastries as desert after the meal.\n\nThe dishes are rather pricy and above mid-range. A dinner for two will cost about 600.000-700.000vnd.\n\nps: They should have different sections for smokers and non-smokers as I don't see no smoking sign anywhere. But to be fair, this goes for most restaurants in Hanoi/Vietnam.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten March 16, 2015",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
